<v Heider Garcia>So there was this one time when one of our watchers came in, and he was like, you know, if I-- he was in a tally room with us, and he said-- this was back in-- I think it was last year. If I were in charge here, I would make all the walls in this room glass, so that you could see where every cable goes, and you could be totally transparent-- something like that.
<v Heider Garcia>有一次，一位观察员进来，他在我们的计票室里，他说——这是在——我想是去年。如果我负责这里，我会让这个房间的所有墙壁都变成玻璃，这样你就可以看到每根电缆的去向，你就可以完全透明——类似这样的。

00:17:10.250 --> 00:17:21.080
<v Heider Garcia>And I looked at him and said, why do you want that? He says, well, because we should know where every wire goes, so we can know if you're connected to the internet or not. And I said, well, but the whole point is to show that the machines are not connected to the internet, right?
