<v Heider Garcia>We're talking about the servers and the tally room, so there shouldn't be any cable going in the machine. So I told him, what about if we rearrange the room, so the machines are not, like, in this little cabinet under the desk, but up where you can see them and you can-- he said, well, maybe that would be a start.
<v Heider Garcia>我们谈论的是服务器和计票室，所以机器里不应该有任何电缆进去。所以我告诉他，如果我们重新布置房间怎么样，机器不再放在桌下的那个小柜子里，而是放在你能看到的地方——他说，嗯，也许那会是一个开始。

00:17:33.920 --> 00:17:41.330
<v Heider Garcia>So the next election, they came back in a runoff. You know, when they walked in the room, I told them, all the machines are on top of the tables. You can see the back. They're against the glass.
<v Heider Garcia>所以在下次决选时，他们又回来了。当他们走进房间时，我告诉他们，所有的机器都在桌子上。你可以看到背面。它们靠在玻璃上。

